    {
      "text": "food shall be for store … against the seven years of famine, Gen. 41:36. he asked them of their welfare, Gen. 43:27. Egyptians … said, Give us bread … for the money faileth, Gen. 47:15. that the poor of thy people may eat, Ex. 23:11. thou shalt not glean … leave them for the poor, Lev. 19:10 (23:22). nor shut thine hand from thy poor brother, Deut. 15:7. sheaf in the field … for the fatherless, and for the widow, Deut. 24:19. to seek the welfare of … Israel, Neh. 2:10. my welfare passeth away as a cloud, Job 30:15. He that giveth unto the poor shall not lack, Prov. 28:27. bring the poor that are cast out to thy house, Isa. 58:7. this man seeketh not the welfare of this people, Jer. 38:4. Bring ye all the tithes into the storehouse, Mal. 3:10 (3 Ne. 24:10).",
