    {
      "text": "That thine alms may be in secret, Matt. 6:4 (3 Ne. 13:4). done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me, Matt. 25:40. brought him to an inn, and took care of him, Luke 10:34. sold their possessions … parted them to all men, as every man had need, Acts 2:45 (4:35). brought a certain part, and laid it at the apostles’ feet, Acts 5:2. their widows were neglected in the daily ministration, Acts 6:1. send relief unto the brethren which dwelt in Judæa, Acts 11:29. contribution for the poor saints, Rom. 15:26. bestow all my goods to feed the poor … and have not charity, 1 Cor. 13:3. any … that believeth have widows, let them relieve them, 1 Tim. 5:16. visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, James 1:27. having compassion one of another, 1 Pet. 3:8.",
