      "text": "he hath sought … your own eternal welfare, 2 Ne. 1:25. I have none other object save it be the everlasting welfare of your souls, 2 Ne. 2:30 (Jacob 2:3; Moro. 6:5). desirous for the welfare of your souls, 2 Ne. 6:3 (Enos 1:9). they seek not the welfare of Zion, 2 Ne. 26:29. thy performance may be for the welfare of thy soul, 2 Ne. 32:9. Nephi … having labored in all his days for their welfare, Jacob 1:10. anxiety for the welfare of your souls, Jacob 2:3. free with your substance, that they may be rich, Jacob 2:17. feel a desire for the welfare of my brethren, Enos 1:9. administer of your substance unto him that standeth in need, Mosiah 4:16. imparting to one another both temporally and spiritually, Mosiah 18:29. filled with pain and anguish for the welfare of their souls, Mosiah 25:11. fasting and mighty prayer in behalf of the welfare of the souls of those who knew not God, Alma 6:6. prayer … for your welfare, Alma 34:27. impart of your substance, if ye have, Alma 34:28. labor … for the welfare … of his people, Alma 48:12. doing all things for the welfare and happiness of his people, Hel. 12:2. had all things common among them, 4 Ne. 1:3. an eye single to his glory, or the welfare of the … long dispersed covenant people, Morm. 8:15.",
